# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-7, 2.1-11). L §3.6: batched "labels them by batch, the movement that brought the units into
# the model's batched places"; "first in, first out | order k.batch.day"; "Batches start here. At a batched place, an
# arrival from a place that keeps no batches starts a batch, the movement m; an arrival from a batched place keeps each
# part's batch." s1 takes 120.00: b1's 100.00, then 20.00 of b2; t1 moves 20.00 of b2 to konto2, which keeps batch b2
# (and t1 starts none). Figures by scratch/exp4.py.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind lots: place PLN min 0
  batched
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order k.batch.day
place konto: lots lives 2026-01-01..
place konto2: lots lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input b1_day: date
input b1_amt: money PLN
input b2_day: date
input b2_amt: money PLN
input s1_day: date
input s1_amt: money PLN
input t1_day: date
input t1_amt: money PLN
move b1: transfers
  on b1_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount b1_amt
move b2: transfers
  on b2_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount b2_amt
move s1: transfers
  on s1_day
  leg cash from konto to shop amount s1_amt
move t1: transfers
  on t1_day
  leg cash from konto to konto2 amount t1_amt
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-04-30), bal(konto, 2026-04-30) of b1, bal(konto, 2026-04-30) of b2, s1.cash.amount of b1, s1.cash.amount of b2
ask q2: bal(konto2, 2026-05-31) of b2, bal(konto2, 2026-05-31) of t1

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[konto2] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  b1_day = 2026-02-01
  b1_amt = 100.00 PLN
  b2_day = 2026-03-01
  b2_amt = 50.00 PLN
  s1_day = 2026-04-01
  s1_amt = 120.00 PLN
  t1_day = 2026-05-01
  t1_amt = 20.00 PLN
=== expect
q: (30.00 PLN, 0.00 PLN, 30.00 PLN, 100.00 PLN, 20.00 PLN)
  cut 2026-01-01
q2: (20.00 PLN, 0.00 PLN)
  cut 2026-01-01
